{"id":"moth","name":"Moth","aliases":["Moth"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:moth","torrey:moth-the"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Moth","text":"Heb. ‘ash, from a root meaning “to fall away,” as moth-eaten garments fall to pieces (Job 4:19; 13:28; Isa. 50:9; 51:8; Hos. 5:12). Gr. ses, thus rendered in Matt. 6:19, 20; Luke 12:33. Allusion is thus made to the destruction of clothing by the larvae of the clothes-moth. This is the only lepidopterous insect referred to in Scripture."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6211","lemma":"עָשׁ","xlit":"ʻâsh","gloss":"a moth","kjv":"moth. See also H5906","count":7,"share":0.7},{"strong":"G4597","lemma":"σής","xlit":"sḗs","gloss":"a moth","kjv":"moth","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"G1358","lemma":"διορύσσω","xlit":"diorýssō","gloss":"to penetrate burglariously","kjv":"break through","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H7538","lemma":"רָקָב","xlit":"râqâb","gloss":"decay","kjv":"rottenness","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"G853","lemma":"ἀφανίζω","xlit":"aphanízō","gloss":"to render unapparent","kjv":"corrupt, disfigure, perish, vanish away","count":2,"share":0.2},{"strong":"G2343","lemma":"θησαυρίζω","xlit":"thēsaurízō","gloss":"to amass or reserve","kjv":"lay up, in store, treasure","count":2,"share":0.2}],"verses":["Job.4.19","Job.13.28","Job.27.18","Ps.39.11","Isa.50.9","Isa.51.8","Hos.5.12","Matt.6.19","Matt.6.20","Jas.5.2"],"related":[{"id":"insects","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.061,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"life","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.021,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"houses","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.02,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"}],"works":[{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Second Century","count":3,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFV.1","count":2,"book":"Fragments","title":""},{"chapter":"ANFX.3","count":1,"book":"The Instructor","title":"Book III"}]},{"work":"ph